# Migration bot: watches the launchpad, publishes live events to Redis and migrates curves that fill.
# Copy to .env (git-ignored: never commit it). The bot reads process.env only: export these, or start it with `node --env-file=.env`.

# --- Required ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which TokenLaunchpad-be/packages/deployments/<name>.json to read (the launchpad to watch).
DEPLOYMENT=local
# JSON-RPC of the chain.
RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
# SECRET. The bot's own wallet: it only ever pays gas (a little ETH is enough). Make one for it (`cast wallet new`): never a wallet that holds
# anything else, and never a well-known test key (the bot refuses those).
BOT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where live events are published for the API's websockets. Without it the bot still migrates, and pages poll instead.
# REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
# How often, in milliseconds, it looks for new blocks.
# POLL_MS=4000
# How often, in minutes, it re-scans for curves that filled without it noticing.
# CATCH_UP_MINUTES=10
# The most blocks one eth_getLogs may cover. Set it to what your RPC plan allows (Alchemy's free plan: 10); unset, thousands.
# LOG_RANGE_BLOCKS=10
